# The readers of keys that are not questions, for tests/check-question-typeahead.sh.
#
# A question reads its answer with wpe_paint_ask_key and keeps nothing typed
# before it.  Every other function that calls wpe_paint_modal_getch, the
# owner's reader for a box of either kind (wpe_paint_box_key), or a wrapper
# that reads for others (e_opt_getch, e_opt_read_key), is listed here with its
# kind and the reason it is that kind.  A function that is not listed fails
# the build: its author says which kind it is.
#
#   keeps|function|reason    a place to type or move; the user asked for it
#                            with a key and its keys are text or movement, so
#                            it keeps what was typed ahead
#   wraps|function|reason    reads for others: the callers are what is
#                            classified, or, at the end of one engine's chain,
#                            the reader below that says whose key it is
#   pending|function|reason  a question that a later pass moves onto the
#                            owner; the line is deleted then
#
# A line that matches nothing is stale and fails.

# ---- menus, prefixes, the File Manager, pickers -----------------------------
keeps|WpeMenuGetch|the menu bar and its dropdowns: arrows and letters
keeps|e_prefix_read_letter|the letter after Ctrl-K, Ctrl-O or Ctrl-Q, typed with the prefix
keeps|e_file_window|the File Manager: its keys are movement and type-ahead into the name
keeps|e_ai_pick|the assistant's pickers (models, scopes): the Down typed before one opens moves it
keeps|ai_mp_run|the model picker
keeps|e_dif_colors|a colour picker
keeps|e_frb_x_menue|a colour picker
keeps|e_frb_t_menue|a colour picker
keeps|e_opt_sec_box|a submenu list: letters and arrows
keeps|e_size_move|Size/Move of a window frame: arrows
keeps|e_opt_move|the keyboard mover of a dialog box: arrows
keeps|e_opt_wait_esc_or_resize|a dialog the screen cannot show: every key is swallowed until Esc or a resize
keeps|e_vterm_user_screen|the User Screen: any key returns, asked for with Alt-F5

# ---- line editors -------------------------------------------------------------
keeps|e_schreib_zif|a one-line field: text is typed in it
keeps|e_schreib_leiste_lines|a line editor: text is typed in it, and Ctrl-O T inside it

# ---- the debugger and language server prefixes and peeks ------------------------
keeps|e_deb_inp|the letter after the Ctrl-G prefix
keeps|e_lsp_cursor_popup|a peek that changes nothing; . and , walk the diagnostics
keeps|e_lsp_hover_show|the letter after Alt-Q in a peek
keeps|e_lsp_signature_show|the letter after Alt-Q in a peek
keeps|e_lsp_ui_jump_diag|the letter after Alt-Q in a peek
keeps|e_lsp_ui_key|the Alt-Q prefix letter

# ---- readers for others ---------------------------------------------------------
# The dialog engine runs a box the user types or moves in (a dialog, a picker)
# and a box that asks a question (a message box) with the same widget loops.
# Which of the two a box is says the question the box carries, and the
# engine's own reader (e_opt_getch) is where the owner reads it, so the loops
# below are listed once, as readers for the engine.
wraps|e_opt_getch|reads the key of a box the engine runs: a message box carries the question, a dialog keeps its type-ahead
wraps|e_opt_read_key|reads the focused widget's key; its callers are classified
wraps|e_opt_run_checkbox|reads one key for the focused checkbox and routes it; the engine's reader says whose key it is
wraps|e_opt_run_radio|reads one key for the focused radio option and routes it; the engine's reader says whose key it is
wraps|e_opt_run_button|reads one key for the focused button and routes it; the engine's reader says whose key it is

# ---- a series the user answers on purpose --------------------------------------
# The "Replace this occurrence?" box of Find/Replace is asked once per hit and
# the user types a row of answers at once, as he types into a field, so it
# keeps its type-ahead.  It reads through the owner like every message box:
# its question is made with WPE_ASK_SERIES, only by e_opt_kst_series (the
# checker's rule d), and e_message_series is the one entry that asks for it.
# It calls no reader, so no line of this file is needed for it.

# ---- questions, listed nowhere here ------------------------------------------------
# e_error_read_answer (an error box), e_opt_box_wait_key (About, System Info
# and the other any-key boxes) and every message box the dialog engine runs
# (close, save, overwrite, quit debugging) read their answer through the
# owner, so no line names them.
